---
/**
 * Colophon: what the type is, what the site is made of, where it was made.
 * A standalone page rather than a hub section: one narrow measure, one small
 * device, no rails.
 *
 * Formatting: Astro drops the newline that follows a closing inline tag, so a
 * line must not begin right after one without an explicit `&#32;` (the
 * "Spectralat 300" bug). The entities below are required.
 */

import { place } from "../../data/about";
import Shell from "../../layouts/Shell.astro";

/**
 * Dev-only until the copy is written. A rest param with an empty
 * getStaticPaths in production makes a static build omit the route entirely;
 * `prerender = false` would only switch it to SSR, and the page would still
 * ship. In production there is no route, link, card or sitemap entry. To
 * publish: return the single path unconditionally, and drop the DEV guard on
 * the corner link in HubShell.
 */
export function getStaticPaths() {
	return import.meta.env.DEV ? [{ params: { slug: undefined } }] : [];
}
---

<Shell
	title="Colophon — Conor Scheidt"
	description="The type, the materials, and the machinery behind crs.so."
	scrollable
>
	<div class="colo">
		<header class="colo-head">
			<a class="colo-back" href="/">← crs.so</a>
			<h1>Colophon</h1>
		</header>

		<div class="colo-body">
			<p>
				Type is <b>Fraunces</b>, cut at optical size 144 for display, set beside
				&#32;<b>Spectral</b> at 300 for reading. <b>JetBrains Mono</b> sets code. Two inks:
				warm black, warm paper. Night exchanges them, which is why the switch costs one
				frame and never fades.
			</p>

			<p>
				The object at the centre is <b>4,600 points</b>. Each position is computed in a
				vertex shader from the parameter of a curve, so there is no geometry buffer and no
				compute pass: one draw call, eighty bytes of uniform. Index is a trefoil knot.
				Projects is the edge set of an icosahedron; Writing, a loxodrome; About, three
				Borromean rings. Changing section interpolates the parameters rather than swapping
				models. Where WebGPU is missing, the same equations run on a canvas at a lower
				count.
			</p>

			<p>
				Built with <b>Astro</b> and TypeScript. Figures in <b>d3</b>, mathematics in
				&#32;<b>KaTeX</b>. The C and C++ in the essays compile in the page: <b>clang</b> and
				&#32;<b>lld</b> built for WebAssembly, eighteen megabytes fetched once and kept. The
				port follows <a href="https://github.com/binji/wasm-clang" rel="noopener">binji&rsquo;s
				wasm-clang</a>. A program that reads standard input blocks on a
				&#32;<code>SharedArrayBuffer</code> until you type, the way it would in a terminal.
			</p>

			<p>
				Static files, served from Cloudflare. No analytics, no third-party requests, no
				cookies. Source at <a href="https://git.crs.so" rel="me">git.crs.so</a>.
			</p>

			<p class="colo-sign">{place.city}</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Shell>
